# Wrangler's local state — the dev-session cache and the uploaded-asset
# manifest. Regenerated on every run, never a source artefact.
#
# `dist/` needs no entry: the repository root already ignores it everywhere.
.wrangler/

# The one place a real Supabase project ref may sit on a developer's machine
# (see README.md). It is a build input, not a secret, but it is still an
# environment fact about one deployment and has no business in the repository —
# `public/_headers` keeps the PROJECT placeholder, always.
#
# The root .gitignore already covers `.env` and `.env.*`; this restates it here
# so the rule is visible in the directory it protects.
.env
.env.*
